  <revision rev="1" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>49c739dcc035aae42cfd592ba64b6899</srcmd5>
    <version>1.8.0</version>
    <time>1785872051</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: github-mcp-server 1.8.0.

GitHub's official Model Context Protocol server, exposing the GitHub API as
MCP tools over stdio and streamable HTTP. Ships the mcpcurl developer tool as
a subpackage and bash/zsh/fish completions.

Deliberate packaging decisions, all documented in the spec and changelog:
 * The bundled MCP App UI (a Vite/TypeScript tree needing several hundred npm
   packages) is not built. Upstream ships a committed placeholder so the
   go:embed directive resolves, and every call site is guarded by
   UIAssetsAvailable(), so the server runs normally without it.
 * Upstream's '-s -w' link flags are dropped so debuginfo is usable.
 * No OAuth client credentials are injected -- those are upstream's own and
   are absent from the source. Disclosed in %description rather than hidden.
 * One patch, sent upstream as github/github-mcp-server#2998: the cobra root
   command was named 'server' instead of after the installed binary, so
   generated shell completions bound to a nonexistent command and never
   fired.

Verified with a local osc build for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64: green,
%check runs the full offline unit suite (28 packages, 0 failures, no network
or token needed), rpmlint 0 errors 0 badness, source_validator clean. The
remaining rpmlint warnings are files-duplicate among the vendored license
texts shipped under %license, which are kept per-dependency on purpose.</comment>
    <requestid>1369275</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
